one of the things i've been talking  about for a few weeks now  is what i see is the underselling of the  coronavirus vaccines  as something that could well be making  people  less interested in getting vaccinated  when you see  endless headlines about even if you're  vaccinated you can't do anything  differently you can't hang out with  people you can't do indoors  you have to wear a mask you can't travel  you can't visit anybody all of this  different stuff  and we've been expecting new guidelines  from the cdc  in conjunction with the dramatically  accelerating vaccination  numbers that we talked about yesterday  and we got it  the big news to skip to sort of the meat  of the announcement  is that the cdc now says vaccinated  people  can safely gather indoors without masks  with  other vaccinated people without social  distancing  you can hug vaccinated people can also  be with unvaccinated people if the  unvaccinated people are of low risk and  there's a few other things let's look at  cdc director uh walensky telling us this  yesterday  cdc recommends that fully vaccinated  people can visit with other  fully vaccinated people in small  gatherings indoors  without wearing masks or physical  distancing remember here we are talking  about  private settings where everyone is  vaccinated  so what does this mean if you and a  friend or you  and a family member are both vaccinated  you can have dinner together  wearing masks without distancing you can  visit your grandparents if you have been  vaccinated  and they have been too now  i want to talk to you about another more  complicated scenario  it involves vaccinated people visiting  with unvaccinated people  when fully vaccinated people visit with  unvaccinated people  we have to consider the underlying risks  of the unvaccinated people  and any unvaccinated members of their  household  we take this approach because all of our  guidance is rooted in making sure we are  keeping  people safe so  cdc recommends that fully vaccinated  people can  visit with unvaccinated people from one  other household indoors without wearing  masks or physical distancing  as long as the unvaccinated people and  any unvaccinated members of their  household  are not at high risk for severe covet 19  disease  so additionally vaccinated people can  gather indoors  unmasked with unvaccinated people  from the same household assuming that  the unvaccinated people  are low risk so the point here is  the vaccines are extremely effective  all essentially 100 effective at  preventing serious covet and death  uh and they appear to reduce  transmission more on that  in a moment and on this basis  it is time for certain elements  to start going in the direction of  re-normalization now  vaccinated people should not go hang out  with a high-risk  85-year-old unvaccinated person  fortunately  increasingly a majority of those over 60  have now been vaccinated at least with  one shot in the united states majority  not all  to put it a different way vaccinated  grandparents  can visit unvaccinated healthy kids and  grandkids  but vaccinated kids should not be  visiting unvaccinated  grandparents um i i will be paying very  close attention to this household thing  being vaccinated myself my girlfriend  being vaccinated i have friends who are  couples and work from home who aren't  yet vaccinated  that seems safe and that's in accordance  with what the cdc says  two couples from different households  especially  if one doesn't work from home i'm not  going to get into that kind of  situation for the foreseeable future so  this is a big step forward  the science seems increasingly clear on  how effective these vaccines are  at preventing death serious illness  increasingly clear that they also reduce  transmissibility  although that's still being studied the  cdc said yesterday  a quote growing body of evidence  suggests people who are vaccinated  are not only less likely to have  asymptomatic infections but also  potentially less likely to transmit the  virus  still they aren't ruling out the  possibility  that a vaccinated person could  inadvertently transmit the virus  we're going to learn more about that  over the coming weeks and months  also from the cdc yesterday vaccinated  people don't need to quarantine or get  tested if they have a known exposure to  the virus  assuming they don't develop symptoms so  this would be  you find out someone you work with if  you're working in an office  someone you work with has tested  positive you are vaccinated  you do not need to go through an  isolation and quarantine protocol if you  are vaccinated  unless you develop a symptom um  vaccinated people  should be avoiding large and medium  gatherings still everybody should  and of course none of these guidelines  change  anything for vaccinated people out in  public if a grocery store says  masks then everyone wears masks  regardless of vaccination stat status  that should be obvious  that makes absolute perfect sense so  hopefully and we're going to have a very  interesting interview later today with  jonathan berman about  the vaccine hesitancy which is  fortunately waning in the united states  on the covet vaccine  hopefully this increases the number of  people who get vaccinated since  the more that that do get vaccinated  number one the more people that can get  into this new protocol  outlined by the cdc but also the faster  we can go to the next step of relaxation  of guidelines now some states are just  relaxing all guidelines now  texas mississippi some other scheduling  further relaxation is going to  wide open everything no masks anywhere  i believe that there will be people who  will want the  vaccine because now it's in black and  white from the cdc you get vaccinated  and your parents do  you can hang out and you can hug and  these are things that  many people in parts of the country  haven't done  for um really almost a year we're about  a week from  the one year mark from the trump  announcement that travel from certain  countries is being banned and sort of  the beginning of  quarantines for those who have been  doing them  that's what's going on in terms of what  vaccinated people can do  let's now go to our weekly covet update  as to the numbers which continue to  improve fortunately  if you are anything like me you probably  aren't thrilled  with the idea of going into a doctor's  office right now and  thankfully there's a practical and  affordable way  to take control of your health and get  personalized  care from the comfort of your home it's  a service called  steady md they're one of our sponsors  you take a quiz  you get matched with a licensed primary  care physician  who understands your health needs you  have a one hour  video call with your new doctor you  establish a meaningful relationship with  them and after that  your doctor is available to you anytime  by text phone  or video chat this is not a random  doctor on call  each doctor at steady md has a limited  number of patients so they actually have  time  to listen to you you get the personal  attention that you deserve  they can do almost everything an  in-person doctor  can do perform medical evaluations talk  to you about health concerns  send prescriptions to your home or local  pharmacy  and anything they can't do online  they'll quickly set you up with  an in-person provider to do things like  blood tests as an example  you don't need insurance it's only 99  bucks a month with  no other fees or copays there are so  many  practical advantages to using steady md  for primary care  and it's also so much more affordable  go to steadymd.com pacman to take the  free quiz see which doctor is right for  you  i took their quiz they matched me with a  doctor who specializes in my particular  health needs and situation the doctor  they gave me  is a really perfect fit for me and my  medical needs there's  no risk no commitment to get started  just click the link right underneath  this video

